INSTRUCTIONS
Read the local status hierarchy before drawing conclusions.
Use the relation chain, not isolated statements.

DESCRIPTION
Domain: Contract reasoning example

KEY
O = OBJECT
R = RELATION
T1 = BINDING
T2 = GUIDING
T3 = DISPUTED

OBJECTS
O001::CONTRACT_CLAUSE
O002::STATUTORY_RULE
O003::PRECEDENT
O004::CONCLUSION

RELATIONS
R001:F=O002;T=O001;Y=LIMITS;S=T1;
R002:F=O003;T=O001;Y=INTERPRETS;S=T2;
R003:F=O001;T=O004;Y=SUPPORTS;S=T2;

VALIDATION
RULE::Before relying on a precedent, check whether another relation limits, distinguishes, or overturns it.
RULE::Do not convert a disputed interpretation into a binding rule.

CONCLUSION
CONCLUSION::Follow the complete relation chain and preserve the declared status hierarchy.
